# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Haikuan Dong et al. (2024). Molecular dynamics simulations of heat transport using machine-learned potentials: A mini-review and tutorial on GPUMD with neuroevolution potentials.
#   Journal of Applied Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0200833  arXiv:2401.16249v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2401.16249v2 (sha256 8e4c83e9bd280204...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 389 (Overview/taxonomy). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/dong2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the tutorial example, crystalline silicon: the PBE
# data set built from strained/perturbed unit cells and 1000 K AIMD (150
# structures), extended by NEP-driven NPT MD snapshots at 100-1000 K
# (250 structures), the NEP models NEP-iteration-1 and NEP-iteration-2
# (default nep.in hyperparameters, cutoffs 5 A, 30 hidden neurons,
# 100,000 generations) with their training and test RMSEs, the two
# reduced-accuracy NEP variants, and the stated MD speed. The review
# tables of MLP applications (Tables I-II) and the graphene comparison
# of Fig. 3 are literature summaries or figure-only.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

